1
00:01:41,789 --> 00:01:49,000
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:51,840
[Episode 8]

3
00:01:56,930 --> 00:02:01,450
[Noticeboard]

4
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,040
Morning.

5
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:08,710
[Class Challenge Leaderboard]

6
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:04,540
Morning, coward.

7
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:13,910
[Honor List]

8
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,710
Early bird today, huh?

9
00:02:13,910 --> 00:02:17,870
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

10
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:15,190
Shen.

11
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,840
Are you still playing the silent game?

12
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,430
I can't even be bothered to talk to you.

13
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:21,280
Coward.

14
00:02:23,150 --> 00:02:24,120
Morning, Zhixia.

15
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:25,250
Morning, Tingting.

16
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:26,680
I dreamt last night

17
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:28,900
that I got thrown off the pendulum ride.

18
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:31,430
I couldn't sleep at all last night.

19
00:02:31,430 --> 00:02:32,800
I think I have insomnia.

20
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,730
Maybe you were just too excited
from playing during the day.

21
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,640
What happened over the weekend?

22
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:42,680
That's what you get

23
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:44,590
for ditching us for piano practice.

24
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:46,960
So it looks like
things are really moving forward

25
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:48,490
between you and Lin Zhixia.

26
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,590
Fine.

27
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:52,560
Since you call yourself

28
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,910
a walking encyclopedia,

29
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:56,040
let me fill you in on the latest gossip.

30
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:59,030
Lin Zhixia and I are good friends now.

31
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,000
What exactly did I miss?

32
00:03:02,430 --> 00:03:03,560
You guys left me out!

33
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,430
Come in.

34
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,590
Director.

35
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:13,810
You wanted to see me?

36
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:15,910
I wanted to

37
00:03:15,910 --> 00:03:16,870
have a chat with you

38
00:03:16,870 --> 00:03:19,360
about your application
for the experimental class.

39
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,520
Lin Zeqiu,

40
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:21,710
I think

41
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,910
you are not quite suitable
for the experimental class.

42
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:25,560
Why?

43
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:26,710
My grades have already...

44
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:27,750
I saw your grades.

45
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:29,210
Look,

46
00:03:29,970 --> 00:03:31,240
your grades this semester have moved up

47
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,000
ten places from last semester.

48
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,710
Excellent! I can see your progress.

49
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:37,910
But with this much progress,
why am I still not getting in?

50
00:03:38,030 --> 00:03:39,310
I know

51
00:03:39,310 --> 00:03:40,590
what you're asking for.

52
00:03:40,590 --> 00:03:43,000
But the school has its own considerations.

53
00:03:43,470 --> 00:03:44,680
You have good grades,

54
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:47,360
but you're still getting less than half

55
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,680
of the final questions right.

56
00:03:48,680 --> 00:03:49,680
Here, take a look.

57
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:56,370
Actually, this experimental class

58
00:03:56,370 --> 00:03:58,970
mainly focuses on the final questions.

59
00:03:59,190 --> 00:04:00,630
I'm afraid you won't be able to keep up,

60
00:04:00,630 --> 00:04:02,560
and it would be too hard to catch up.

61
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:03,680
So,

62
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,430
I'd suggest

63
00:04:06,630 --> 00:04:09,280
skipping the experimental class for now.

64
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,730
Here, take your application back.

65
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:15,360
Director, I really want to
get into the experimental class.

66
00:04:15,750 --> 00:04:17,360
Lin Zeqiu.

67
00:04:17,950 --> 00:04:19,310
Don't get the wrong idea.

68
00:04:19,310 --> 00:04:22,840
Success isn't just about
getting into the experimental class.

69
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,330
Say I let you in,

70
00:04:25,330 --> 00:04:26,460
but you can't keep up

71
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:28,010
and really struggle, what then?

72
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:29,810
You'd have to transfer back out.

73
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:32,610
Wouldn't that be a huge blow
to your confidence?

74
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:34,670
Don't you think?

75
00:04:36,330 --> 00:04:38,590
You know Jin Baihui from Grade 10, right?

76
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:41,180
She got into
that elite program in Beijing.

77
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,980
And you know what? She couldn't
keep up and had to transfer back.

78
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:44,640
She even got held back a grade!

79
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:49,420
Director, please...

80
00:04:49,420 --> 00:04:51,550
Can't you just give me another chance?

81
00:04:52,370 --> 00:04:53,810
Lin Zeqiu.

82
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:56,659
You are absolutely a promising student.

83
00:04:56,659 --> 00:04:58,100
Just keep up this steady pace,

84
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,060
and you'll definitely
get into your dream university.

85
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,980
As for those final questions,

86
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,860
I've found a great teacher
to help you out.

87
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:08,660
May I come in?

88
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:12,220
Yes, it's Lin Zhixia.

89
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,420
I'll be going now, Director.

90
00:05:37,330 --> 00:05:39,690
Brother, what are you so angry about?

91
00:05:43,330 --> 00:05:44,530
You're a big shot now,

92
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:47,790
acting like my teacher
right in front of the teacher.

93
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,690
I told Director Sui

94
00:05:52,010 --> 00:05:54,130
that you definitely
wouldn't let me tutor you.

95
00:05:54,130 --> 00:05:55,570
I only came because he said

96
00:05:55,570 --> 00:05:57,230
he'd talk some sense into you.

97
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:01,540
Besides, I really can help you
with the final questions.

98
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:05,830
I don't need your help.

99
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,370
Brother, wait.

100
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:18,480
You left the office in such a hurry.

101
00:06:18,810 --> 00:06:19,680
Director Sui asked me

102
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,810
to return your application
for the experimental class.

103
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:26,840
I don't want it.

104
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,310
Throw it away for me.

105
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:29,770
Also,

106
00:06:30,770 --> 00:06:32,860
don't call me brother at school.

107
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:54,930
Lin Zhixia.

108
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:09,900
Why aren't you going back to class?

109
00:07:13,450 --> 00:07:15,450
Hurry up, you're going to be late.

110
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:22,330
Let's continue.

111
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,100
Regarding the changes

112
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:25,010
in this graph,

113
00:07:25,010 --> 00:07:26,670
and the t-axis, specifically

114
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:27,690
whether v is positive or negative,

115
00:07:27,690 --> 00:07:29,490
does anyone have any questions?

116
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:32,220
Alright. Now that
we're clear on this, let's move on.

117
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:33,570
The direction of motion

118
00:07:33,570 --> 00:07:35,500
depends on which quadrant it's in.

119
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:37,370
When v is above the t-axis, it's positive;

120
00:07:37,370 --> 00:07:38,300
and when it's below the t-axis...

121
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,100
Lin Zhixia.

122
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,420
What's

123
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:42,770
in that envelope?

124
00:07:43,890 --> 00:07:44,690
Nothing.

125
00:07:48,690 --> 00:07:50,250
I saw everything today.

126
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:55,100
Besides, aren't we best friends?

127
00:07:57,890 --> 00:08:01,010
Can I just take a peek at it?

128
00:08:03,570 --> 00:08:04,900
Sorry, I really can't.

129
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,300
The larger the k value is,

130
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,180
the greater

131
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:11,860
the acceleration a

132
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:12,770
it represents.

133
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:14,930
Lin.

134
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:20,300
I have a few words I want to say to you.

135
00:08:23,930 --> 00:08:24,930
I don't like

136
00:08:25,810 --> 00:08:27,610
girls who only know how to study.

137
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:30,250
But I've really liked you
for a very long time.

138
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:32,610
If you think
I'm too focused on my studies,

139
00:08:33,580 --> 00:08:35,220
I can change for you.

140
00:08:35,409 --> 00:08:37,140
I'll stop studying, I promise!

141
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,370
No.

142
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:42,100
No way.

143
00:08:43,890 --> 00:08:45,170
Lin, hold on a second.

144
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:51,290
This is how I feel.

145
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:53,340
It's all in the letter.

146
00:08:54,130 --> 00:08:55,620
Please read it carefully.

147
00:08:55,890 --> 00:08:57,370
Just keep it.

148
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:00,050
And

149
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:02,250
leave me alone from now on.

150
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:06,530
Lin Zhixia.

151
00:10:08,370 --> 00:10:09,170
What's wrong?

152
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:11,180
You look totally spaced out.

153
00:10:12,250 --> 00:10:13,980
It's all because of my brother.

154
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,410
Lin Zeqiu?

155
00:10:16,410 --> 00:10:17,580
Don't point.

156
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:21,900
He doesn't want me to say
he's my brother at school.

157
00:10:22,010 --> 00:10:22,820
Why?

158
00:10:25,130 --> 00:10:26,410
He's just being shy.

159
00:10:31,740 --> 00:10:33,200
I mean, he's annoying too,

160
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:35,720
but please don't tell anyone
he's my brother.

161
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:37,250
He'll nag me if he finds out.

162
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,050
Why?

163
00:10:40,220 --> 00:10:42,050
Why does he get to decide?

164
00:10:42,370 --> 00:10:43,740
If I had a sister like you,

165
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:45,800
I'd be shouting it from the rooftops.

166
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:47,270
But he won't even say you're his sister?

167
00:10:47,270 --> 00:10:48,100
No way.

168
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:49,860
I'm taking you to confront him.

169
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:50,660
Confront him?

170
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:53,650
Right now,
while everyone's around during the break.

171
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:54,250
This

172
00:10:54,250 --> 00:10:56,380
needs to be sorted out once and for all.

173
00:10:57,860 --> 00:10:58,650
Zhixia.

174
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:00,580
Is that the guy you like?

175
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:02,050
Don't point.

176
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:04,340
What if someone notices?

177
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:07,770
He is really handsome and charming.

178
00:11:08,530 --> 00:11:10,190
Why don't you just go tell him?

179
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:11,460
There's no time like the present.

180
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:12,460
Let's do it today.

181
00:11:12,530 --> 00:11:13,530
No.

182
00:11:14,170 --> 00:11:16,370
I'm not ready yet.

183
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,460
Besides, what if I get rejected

184
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:20,460
in front of all these people?

185
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:22,410
Come on!

186
00:11:22,430 --> 00:11:23,290
No.

187
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:24,980
I already promised him.

188
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:26,010
No, you won't.

189
00:11:26,010 --> 00:11:27,410
Let's go.

190
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:28,220
I don't want to.

191
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:29,220
-No.
-Come on.

192
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:30,250
Let's go.

193
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:32,130
I really can't.
He'll be furious if I go over.

194
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:32,860
Lin Zhixia.

195
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:38,740
I...

196
00:11:41,050 --> 00:11:42,650
I have a question I can't solve.

197
00:11:42,650 --> 00:11:43,710
Help me take a look.

198
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:05,370
Lin Zhixia.

199
00:12:06,410 --> 00:12:08,220
Is something bothering you?

200
00:12:09,250 --> 00:12:10,050
No.

201
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,410
I just feel that...

202
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:18,700
Life is long,

203
00:12:19,130 --> 00:12:20,730
and we will meet many people.

204
00:12:21,130 --> 00:12:21,980
But,

205
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,580
we should do what is appropriate

206
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:24,820
for our age.

207
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:26,220
At our age,

208
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:28,130
the most important thing is studying.

209
00:12:28,130 --> 00:12:29,650
So we can't let anything

210
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:31,580
interfere with our studies.

211
00:12:34,940 --> 00:12:36,800
Why are you suddenly saying this?

212
00:12:38,050 --> 00:12:39,170
I know that.

213
00:12:43,290 --> 00:12:44,250
Glad you know.

214
00:12:50,790 --> 00:12:53,610
[Astronomy Club Recruitment]

215
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:07,890
[Astronomy Club Recruitment]

216
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:17,470
[Astronomy Club Recruitment]

217
00:13:17,570 --> 00:13:19,950
[Astronomy Club]

218
00:13:35,050 --> 00:13:35,860
What is it?

219
00:13:37,410 --> 00:13:39,270
I want to join the astronomy club.

220
00:13:40,050 --> 00:13:40,860
Your reason?

221
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:43,820
I'm very interested in astronomy.

222
00:13:43,820 --> 00:13:45,500
I've loved watching the stars
since I was little.

223
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:46,410
I've even read

224
00:13:47,250 --> 00:13:49,940
The Flammarion Book of Astronomy.

225
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:50,890
Really?

226
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:53,620
Then tell me, last Wednesday night,

227
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:56,720
what was the brightest star
next to the moon called?

228
00:14:01,340 --> 00:14:01,980
Po...

229
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:03,740
Polaris.

230
00:14:03,890 --> 00:14:05,100
Last Wednesday was a new moon.

231
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:06,500
You couldn't see the moon at all.

232
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:07,650
Polaris is always due north.

233
00:14:07,650 --> 00:14:08,940
It can't possibly be next to the moon.

234
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:10,250
So what exactly is your reason

235
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:12,050
for joining the astronomy club?

236
00:14:14,130 --> 00:14:15,620
I just want to join.

237
00:14:15,770 --> 00:14:17,580
Everyone can join the astronomy club.

238
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:18,700
It's my right.

239
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,290
Let me correct you.

240
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:23,700
Not everyone can join the astronomy club,

241
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:26,290
but everyone can apply for it.

242
00:14:26,890 --> 00:14:27,820
However, deciding whether someone

243
00:14:27,820 --> 00:14:29,290
is qualified to join

244
00:14:29,290 --> 00:14:31,100
is my duty as the vice president.

245
00:14:34,050 --> 00:14:36,700
Have you heard of
that girl named Lin Zhixia?

246
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,640
Yeah, why? What's up with her?

247
00:14:39,770 --> 00:14:41,220
I heard her IQ is super high.

248
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:43,010
She's been top of her class
since she was little,

249
00:14:43,010 --> 00:14:45,460
and she's amazing at
mathematical modeling.

250
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:46,100
Is she?

251
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:48,830
Isn't our club short of people?

252
00:14:48,890 --> 00:14:50,740
If she could join our club,

253
00:14:50,890 --> 00:14:53,100
at the year-end club selection,

254
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,760
we'd definitely win an award.

255
00:14:54,860 --> 00:14:56,890
She's a good student,

256
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:59,220
but that doesn't mean
she knows anything about astronomy.

257
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:00,410
Maybe she's just

258
00:15:00,410 --> 00:15:02,500
a naturally gifted all-rounder.

259
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:05,740
We're an astronomy club,

260
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:06,500
not a training class.

261
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:07,900
Not just anyone can join.

262
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,320
Why are you overreacting?

263
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,130
No, I mean,

264
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:16,210
our recruitment flyers
are already out there.

265
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:17,460
We'll definitely
get some promising students,

266
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,790
so don't worry too much.

267
00:15:20,010 --> 00:15:21,980
Well, you're the vice president.

268
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:23,770
Go find Lin Zhixia and ask her.

269
00:15:23,770 --> 00:15:25,820
If she's willing, that's great.

270
00:15:25,820 --> 00:15:27,240
If not,

271
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:28,740
we won't force her.

272
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:31,130
Me?

273
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:32,170
It's all for the club,

274
00:15:32,170 --> 00:15:33,250
so don't refuse.

275
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,100
I'm leaving.

276
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:04,950
What's wrong, Brother?

277
00:16:05,050 --> 00:16:05,860
Nothing.

278
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:09,620
I just came out to get some water.

279
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:18,580
Got a question for me?

280
00:16:19,130 --> 00:16:19,940
No.

281
00:16:20,290 --> 00:16:21,620
I'm just thirsty.

282
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:23,580
Go on.

283
00:16:46,770 --> 00:16:48,980
I just saw on the notice board

284
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:51,500
that the astronomy club is recruiting.

285
00:16:51,770 --> 00:16:52,650
I didn't know our school

286
00:16:52,650 --> 00:16:54,460
had such an advanced club.

287
00:16:56,130 --> 00:16:57,820
What, isn't the basketball team
keeping you busy enough?

288
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:59,370
Now you're into astronomy too?

289
00:16:59,370 --> 00:17:02,130
How could I even dream of
joining such an advanced club?

290
00:17:02,130 --> 00:17:03,890
Lin Zhixia, I just think

291
00:17:03,890 --> 00:17:05,619
this is quite suitable for you.

292
00:17:05,619 --> 00:17:11,290
[Please Keep Quiet in the Library]

293
00:17:07,740 --> 00:17:10,460
I haven't thought about
joining a club, actually.

294
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:11,770
But we've always had a subscription

295
00:17:11,770 --> 00:17:13,010
to astronomy magazines.

296
00:17:12,829 --> 00:17:15,859
[Please Keep Quiet in the Library]

297
00:17:14,010 --> 00:17:15,740
The astronomy club...

298
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:18,310
sounds pretty cool.

299
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:19,220
Right?

300
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:33,680
The starlight in your eyes

301
00:17:35,290 --> 00:17:37,460
is the atoms born 13.8 billion years ago

302
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:39,850
during the Big Bang,

303
00:17:40,570 --> 00:17:41,980
traveling through time and space

304
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:45,180
just to light up my eyes at this moment.

305
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:01,290
Lin Zhixia?

306
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:06,330
You must be Lin Zhixia.

307
00:18:08,250 --> 00:18:11,050
I'm Ye Wenxi,
the president of the astronomy club.

308
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:12,180
Hello.

309
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:13,010
Hello.

310
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,050
I really want you

311
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:16,580
to join our astronomy club.

312
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:18,610
I heard you're also very good at math.

313
00:18:18,610 --> 00:18:21,090
Actually, the core of astronomy is math.

314
00:18:21,220 --> 00:18:23,750
I think you fit the vibe
of our club perfectly.

315
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:25,420
I'm not sure

316
00:18:25,770 --> 00:18:27,850
if I have the energy to join a club.

317
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:31,290
President.

318
00:18:31,740 --> 00:18:34,050
Is your astronomy club basically just

319
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:35,820
about stargazing and stuff?

320
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:40,180
Of course,
observation is a huge part of it.

321
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:42,010
But we also have

322
00:18:42,010 --> 00:18:42,980
our ultimate trump card,

323
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:44,510
which we don't easily show.

324
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:46,810
We have
an intern observation access account

325
00:18:46,810 --> 00:18:48,770
for the Purple Mountain Observatory.

326
00:18:48,770 --> 00:18:49,240
Really?

327
00:18:49,290 --> 00:18:50,020
Yes, really.

328
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:54,770
But it's strictly for club members only.

329
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,180
Don't hesitate.

330
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,700
I asked Lin Zeqiu to find you

331
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,900
just so you could join us
as soon as possible.

332
00:19:03,900 --> 00:19:05,380
He didn't mention it to me.

333
00:19:05,530 --> 00:19:06,460
He didn't?

334
00:19:06,850 --> 00:19:08,380
Impossible. I told him.

335
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,050
It doesn't matter.

336
00:19:13,050 --> 00:19:15,780
I'm officially inviting you
to join our club now.

337
00:19:17,810 --> 00:19:19,220
Then let me think about it.

338
00:19:19,220 --> 00:19:19,940
Okay.

339
00:19:20,330 --> 00:19:22,990
The astronomy club's door
is always open to you.

340
00:19:29,610 --> 00:19:30,940
The president invited you personally.

341
00:19:30,940 --> 00:19:31,850
What's there to think about?

342
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:33,010
Don't you want to go?

343
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:36,420
I do want to go.

344
00:19:41,330 --> 00:19:42,140
But what if...

345
00:19:43,330 --> 00:19:44,570
I mean, what if

346
00:19:45,290 --> 00:19:46,950
someone doesn't want me to go?

347
00:19:48,090 --> 00:19:50,140
Who dares to stop you? Let him try.

348
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:51,660
I'll go straight to him

349
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:53,140
and reason with him.

350
00:19:53,850 --> 00:19:55,510
There really is such a person.

351
00:19:58,360 --> 00:19:59,820
It's fine, I'll handle it.

352
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:01,770
Who? Come on, tell me!

353
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,180
Do your homework.

354
00:20:05,810 --> 00:20:06,700
Oh, I forgot.

355
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:22,360
Tang Tingting.

356
00:20:22,850 --> 00:20:24,180
Can I ask you something?

357
00:20:24,420 --> 00:20:25,350
Yeah, what is it?

358
00:20:28,460 --> 00:20:29,570
Is something

359
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:31,620
going on with Lin Zhixia?

360
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:35,290
Did you notice something?

361
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,940
I just think
she's been acting weird lately.

362
00:20:38,940 --> 00:20:41,740
Does it have anything to do
with an upperclassman?

363
00:20:41,940 --> 00:20:42,740
No!

364
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:45,090
I mean, it's no big deal, really.

365
00:20:45,330 --> 00:20:46,730
So something did happen?

366
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:49,660
I promised her

367
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:52,460
I wouldn't tell anyone
about their relationship.

368
00:20:52,570 --> 00:20:54,570
Relationship? What relationship?

369
00:20:56,610 --> 00:20:57,900
Why don't you ask her?

370
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:03,380
She used to

371
00:21:04,180 --> 00:21:05,910
tell me everything right away.

372
00:21:06,980 --> 00:21:08,310
But this time, nothing.

373
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:09,830
I was just wondering

374
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:12,200
if she was keeping something from me.

375
00:21:13,290 --> 00:21:14,610
She's super smart,

376
00:21:14,740 --> 00:21:16,800
but she trusts people way too easily.

377
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:20,380
I'm afraid she's being taken advantage of.

378
00:21:22,330 --> 00:21:23,420
I think

379
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,530
she kept it from you

380
00:21:24,530 --> 00:21:26,460
because it's her own business.

381
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,380
I mean, we're all teenagers.

382
00:21:28,570 --> 00:21:30,610
It's totally normal
for things like this to happen.

383
00:21:30,610 --> 00:21:31,570
But you don't need to worry too much.

384
00:21:31,570 --> 00:21:32,650
She won't be taken advantage of.

385
00:21:32,650 --> 00:21:33,810
I've already given her some advice.

386
00:21:33,810 --> 00:21:35,340
It should be resolved soon.

387
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:37,180
Alright.

388
00:21:38,220 --> 00:21:40,420
If she needs any help,

389
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:43,270
please let me know right away.

390
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:52,010
Something still feels off.

391
00:21:59,980 --> 00:22:00,770
Lin Zeqiu.

392
00:22:08,050 --> 00:22:09,000
What are you doing here?

393
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:09,940
Go.

394
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:14,380
What's wrong?

395
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:19,660
The president of your astronomy club
asked you to recruit me.

396
00:22:19,660 --> 00:22:21,050
Why didn't you tell me?

397
00:22:23,330 --> 00:22:24,930
Are you trying to keep me out?

398
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:26,700
I'm afraid that

399
00:22:27,090 --> 00:22:27,980
if we're in the same club,

400
00:22:27,980 --> 00:22:30,570
it'll be too easy for people
to figure out we're siblings.

401
00:22:30,570 --> 00:22:33,700
So just because you're
afraid of being found out, you...

402
00:22:34,810 --> 00:22:37,250
you're killing your own sister's passion?

403
00:22:37,570 --> 00:22:39,010
I didn't mean that.

404
00:22:39,810 --> 00:22:40,610
How about this?

405
00:22:40,610 --> 00:22:42,140
You join, and I'll quit, okay?

406
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:42,940
No!

407
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:45,570
You love astronomy just as much as I do.

408
00:22:45,570 --> 00:22:46,810
I don't want you to give up for me.

409
00:22:46,810 --> 00:22:48,290
It's not about giving up.

410
00:22:48,530 --> 00:22:49,220
I...

411
00:22:49,900 --> 00:22:52,160
Anyway, we just can't be in the same club.

412
00:22:52,420 --> 00:22:53,090
Brother,

413
00:22:54,010 --> 00:22:56,530
the real issue isn't the club.

414
00:22:56,810 --> 00:22:57,980
It's that you're trying to hide the fact

415
00:22:57,980 --> 00:22:59,250
that we're siblings.

416
00:22:59,250 --> 00:23:00,570
I just don't get it.

417
00:23:00,570 --> 00:23:01,660
Why are you so afraid of

418
00:23:01,660 --> 00:23:03,420
people knowing I'm your sister?

419
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:04,900
Keep it down! People are gonna hear us!

420
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:05,460
Let them hear!

421
00:23:05,460 --> 00:23:06,700
Once everyone knows I'm your sister,

422
00:23:06,700 --> 00:23:07,850
problem solved!

423
00:23:07,850 --> 00:23:08,460
Okay.

424
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:10,250
Can I explain it to you properly?

425
00:23:10,250 --> 00:23:12,010
Now is not the time to talk about this.

426
00:23:12,010 --> 00:23:14,140
This is a very direct way
to solve the problem.

427
00:23:14,140 --> 00:23:15,250
Go tell your classmates.

428
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:16,140
If you won't, I will.

429
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:17,250
No. Let's go somewhere else.

430
00:23:17,250 --> 00:23:18,810
I'll explain it to you properly
somewhere else.

431
00:23:18,810 --> 00:23:19,380
Let's go.

432
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:20,380
You always do this.

433
00:23:20,380 --> 00:23:21,050
I'll explain it to you.

434
00:23:21,050 --> 00:23:21,850
-Why?
-Let's go somewhere else.

435
00:23:21,850 --> 00:23:22,900
I'll explain it to you somewhere else.

436
00:23:22,900 --> 00:23:23,740
Just say it right here.

437
00:23:23,740 --> 00:23:25,270
Not here. Please, not here.

438
00:23:25,440 --> 00:23:26,970
Why are you bullying a girl?

439
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:29,010
What's it to you?

440
00:23:29,010 --> 00:23:30,290
So you think you're right to bully her?

441
00:23:30,290 --> 00:23:31,420
Who's bullying her?

442
00:23:31,610 --> 00:23:33,010
You bother Lin Zhixia every day, okay?

443
00:23:33,010 --> 00:23:34,420
You're the one bothering her!

444
00:23:34,420 --> 00:23:34,980
Say that again.

445
00:23:34,980 --> 00:23:36,010
I've been sick of you for a long time.

446
00:23:36,010 --> 00:23:37,180
I'm sick of you too.

447
00:23:37,180 --> 00:23:38,290
What? You wanna fight?

448
00:23:38,290 --> 00:23:38,850
Bring it on!

449
00:23:38,850 --> 00:23:40,310
Lin Zeqiu, we'll help you.

450
00:23:41,810 --> 00:23:43,350
What, you think having more guys
makes you tough?

451
00:23:43,350 --> 00:23:45,270
-Yeah, it does.
-Sophomores bullying people, huh?

452
00:23:45,270 --> 00:23:46,440
Stop fighting!

453
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,780
-Bad news!
-Watch my broom skill!

454
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,090
Jiang Yubai is fighting
with the sophomores!

455
00:23:50,090 --> 00:23:51,140
Who cares if they're sophomores?

456
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:52,500
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

457
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,250
Stop fighting!

458
00:23:56,550 --> 00:23:57,410
Stop fighting!

459
00:23:57,590 --> 00:23:58,920
Stop fighting!

460
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:00,440
Brother.

461
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,100
Duan Qiyan.

462
00:24:01,270 --> 00:24:02,200
You're here too?

463
00:24:02,290 --> 00:24:03,480
Watch yourself. Don't get hurt.

464
00:24:03,480 --> 00:24:04,570
You too. Stay safe.

465
00:24:13,940 --> 00:24:14,940
Stop fighting!

466
00:24:15,140 --> 00:24:16,460
Calm down, everyone!

467
00:24:20,220 --> 00:24:21,050
At that time,

468
00:24:21,250 --> 00:24:22,550
I stood outside the crowd,

469
00:24:22,550 --> 00:24:24,210
watching this chaotic scene.

470
00:24:24,790 --> 00:24:26,850
I suddenly felt it was absurd and sad.

471
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:30,050
Because of this unprovoked broom fight,

472
00:24:30,050 --> 00:24:32,290
my friends and I ended up

473
00:24:32,290 --> 00:24:33,820
getting publicly scolded.

474
00:24:34,350 --> 00:24:35,150
And of course,

475
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:36,480
Lin Zeqiu too.

476
00:24:37,750 --> 00:24:38,950
But I've always known

477
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:41,920
that Zeqiu and I shouldn't be like this.

478
00:24:42,850 --> 00:24:44,070
I just don't get it.

479
00:24:44,850 --> 00:24:46,830
What exactly is wrong

480
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:48,440
between Zeqiu and me?

481
00:25:01,010 --> 00:25:04,220
I actually knew
Lin Zeqiu was your brother all along.

482
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:06,940
No way.

483
00:25:07,660 --> 00:25:09,740
You didn't seem to know at all.

484
00:25:14,570 --> 00:25:15,420
You guys

485
00:25:16,050 --> 00:25:18,380
don't act like normal brother and sister.

486
00:25:22,090 --> 00:25:23,530
He wasn't like this before.

487
00:25:23,530 --> 00:25:24,730
He was very good to me.

488
00:25:25,050 --> 00:25:26,050
When we were kids,

489
00:25:26,740 --> 00:25:29,250
his friends would always
come over to play with him.

490
00:25:29,250 --> 00:25:30,710
He really wanted to go out,

491
00:25:31,250 --> 00:25:33,510
but I didn't have many friends back then.

492
00:25:33,530 --> 00:25:35,530
So I would beg him to stay home with me.

493
00:25:35,530 --> 00:25:36,900
He would actually stay home

494
00:25:36,900 --> 00:25:38,960
and play cat's cradle with me all day.

495
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:40,250
Cat's cradle?

496
00:25:42,770 --> 00:25:43,970
What a great brother.

497
00:25:48,090 --> 00:25:49,690
There was also this one time,

498
00:25:49,770 --> 00:25:51,460
he thought he was dying,

499
00:25:51,610 --> 00:25:52,940
so he wrote a will.

500
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:54,740
It said,

501
00:25:55,610 --> 00:25:57,460
"My sister is a crybaby.

502
00:25:57,940 --> 00:26:00,850
Mom, Dad, please look out for her

503
00:26:00,850 --> 00:26:01,850
and comfort her."

504
00:26:02,330 --> 00:26:03,140
Also,

505
00:26:03,420 --> 00:26:05,850
he left his favorite piggy bank

506
00:26:05,850 --> 00:26:06,740
and car model

507
00:26:06,740 --> 00:26:07,810
to me.

508
00:26:08,500 --> 00:26:10,740
Later, no matter how bad his temper was

509
00:26:10,740 --> 00:26:11,900
or how mean his words were,

510
00:26:11,900 --> 00:26:13,460
whenever I thought of this,

511
00:26:13,810 --> 00:26:14,900
I felt

512
00:26:15,530 --> 00:26:16,860
he definitely loved me.

513
00:26:19,090 --> 00:26:20,530
When did you

514
00:26:20,530 --> 00:26:22,420
start drifting apart?

515
00:26:23,330 --> 00:26:25,260
Probably after we started school.

516
00:26:26,740 --> 00:26:29,340
He was probably
just stressed out from school,

517
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:31,140
so he barely spoke to me.

518
00:26:32,050 --> 00:26:33,250
He studied very hard,

519
00:26:33,740 --> 00:26:35,010
always staying up until midnight.

520
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:36,220
I felt bad for him.

521
00:26:36,570 --> 00:26:37,850
I always wanted to tutor him

522
00:26:37,850 --> 00:26:38,780
and help him out.

523
00:26:39,050 --> 00:26:41,250
But he would be incredibly fierce to me.

524
00:26:42,420 --> 00:26:44,140
After I went to high school,

525
00:26:44,250 --> 00:26:45,700
it got even worse.

526
00:26:46,290 --> 00:26:48,820
The night before school started,
he warned me

527
00:26:49,290 --> 00:26:51,290
not to call him my brother at school.

528
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:53,740
I really don't understand why.

529
00:26:56,570 --> 00:26:58,030
After hearing your story,

530
00:26:58,570 --> 00:27:00,010
I think I know why.

531
00:27:01,660 --> 00:27:02,420
Why?

532
00:27:05,090 --> 00:27:06,090
Maybe because of

533
00:27:07,130 --> 00:27:07,740
his pride.

534
00:27:07,850 --> 00:27:08,460
Pride?

535
00:27:08,940 --> 00:27:09,590
Why?

536
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:13,640
Having such an excellent younger sister

537
00:27:13,740 --> 00:27:15,460
must be quite stressful.

538
00:27:16,810 --> 00:27:17,670
Think about it.

539
00:27:18,050 --> 00:27:19,500
I used to feel pressured

540
00:27:19,500 --> 00:27:20,940
because of your excellence too.

541
00:27:20,940 --> 00:27:23,070
I felt that only by catching up with you

542
00:27:23,500 --> 00:27:25,830
would I be qualified
to stand by your side.

543
00:27:25,980 --> 00:27:27,980
Your brother must feel the same way.

544
00:27:28,050 --> 00:27:30,090
He hopes that one day he can be worthy of

545
00:27:30,090 --> 00:27:32,020
the title of Lin Zhixia's brother.

546
00:27:33,010 --> 00:27:34,810
I think only then will he proudly

547
00:27:34,850 --> 00:27:36,980
shout it from the rooftops.

548
00:27:39,850 --> 00:27:40,810
Really?

549
00:27:56,700 --> 00:27:57,330
Look.

550
00:27:57,940 --> 00:27:59,270
Do they look like stars?

551
00:28:01,660 --> 00:28:02,860
A long, long time ago,

552
00:28:03,330 --> 00:28:05,050
when people connected stars

553
00:28:05,220 --> 00:28:06,620
to form constellations,

554
00:28:07,140 --> 00:28:09,400
they chose stars of similar brightness.

555
00:28:10,310 --> 00:28:11,170
Think about it.

556
00:28:11,590 --> 00:28:13,200
If the person you love

557
00:28:13,310 --> 00:28:15,750
is the brightest star in the night sky,

558
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:17,480
of course you'd want to work hard

559
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:18,940
to shine just as brightly.

560
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:22,860
That way, you can be discovered
at the same time,

561
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:23,750
be defined,

562
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:27,260
and exist in the same constellation.

563
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:34,110
I get it.

564
00:28:37,110 --> 00:28:38,400
I need to find some time

565
00:28:38,830 --> 00:28:40,360
to have a real talk with him.

566
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:41,880
But I need to

567
00:28:43,400 --> 00:28:45,240
figure out the right way to do it.

568
00:28:47,270 --> 00:28:48,200
You are so smart.

569
00:28:48,480 --> 00:28:50,140
I'm sure you can figure it out.

570
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:02,200
Jiang Yubai.

571
00:29:02,750 --> 00:29:04,210
I've realized something.

572
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:09,350
I feel happy seeing you every day.

573
00:29:10,550 --> 00:29:12,550
I am just an ordinary deep learning

574
00:29:12,550 --> 00:29:14,150
artificial neural network.

575
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:16,720
My objective function

576
00:29:16,920 --> 00:29:19,750
is simply to maximize my own happiness.

577
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:22,310
Whenever I lean towards you,

578
00:29:23,240 --> 00:29:24,640
I get positive feedback.

579
00:29:24,720 --> 00:29:25,480
So...

580
00:29:25,480 --> 00:29:26,440
So, Lin Zhixia,

581
00:29:27,810 --> 00:29:28,740
get to the point.

582
00:29:35,070 --> 00:29:35,930
You're so nice.

583
00:29:40,880 --> 00:29:42,270
I try.

584
00:29:54,310 --> 00:29:56,240
What are you doing with that brush?

585
00:29:58,110 --> 00:29:59,310
What do you want to do?

586
00:30:01,880 --> 00:30:04,070
What are you doing? Are you crazy?

587
00:30:04,160 --> 00:30:05,480
I'm going to wipe all this out!

588
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:06,790
Stop it! Stop it!

589
00:30:06,790 --> 00:30:07,790
Why?

590
00:30:09,590 --> 00:30:10,920
What are you doing?

591
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:13,550
Stop it!

592
00:30:15,310 --> 00:30:16,110
Give it to me!

593
00:30:16,230 --> 00:30:16,920
Give it to me!

594
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:18,510
Let go! Let go!

595
00:30:18,510 --> 00:30:19,830
Ouch... my hand!

596
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:23,680
I...

597
00:30:23,790 --> 00:30:25,270
Did I hurt your hand?

598
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:28,920
I didn't mean it,

599
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:30,110
but you were wrong in the first place.

600
00:30:30,110 --> 00:30:32,110
Why did you mess with that painting?

601
00:30:32,350 --> 00:30:33,510
We painted that together
when we were kids.

602
00:30:33,510 --> 00:30:34,710
What if you ruined it?

603
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:36,480
I don't want to be your sister anymore.

604
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:37,940
I want to cut ties with you.

605
00:30:39,920 --> 00:30:41,450
What are you talking about?

606
00:30:41,750 --> 00:30:42,680
What do you mean?

607
00:30:42,790 --> 00:30:44,440
Other brothers know how to spoil

608
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:45,110
and protect their sisters.

609
00:30:45,110 --> 00:30:47,440
And you? You never
have a nice thing to say to me.

610
00:30:47,440 --> 00:30:49,270
I don't mind
that my classmates don't play with me,

611
00:30:49,270 --> 00:30:51,240
but my own brother
avoids me, pushes me away,

612
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:52,160
and hates me.

613
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:54,160
What did I do wrong?

614
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:55,860
Am I that embarrassing to you?

615
00:30:59,270 --> 00:31:00,480
Let me explain.

616
00:31:00,480 --> 00:31:01,750
I don't think that way.

617
00:31:06,550 --> 00:31:07,480
I feel like

618
00:31:10,590 --> 00:31:11,880
I embarrassed you.

619
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:17,020
Look, you're such a good student.

620
00:31:17,110 --> 00:31:18,910
You study for just a few minutes,

621
00:31:19,790 --> 00:31:21,650
and I have to study all night long.

622
00:31:22,720 --> 00:31:24,160
We share the same parents

623
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:25,200
and the same genes,

624
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:27,530
but I just feel like
I'm not as smart as you.

625
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,790
Being dumb just means working harder.

626
00:31:33,640 --> 00:31:34,880
I thought one day

627
00:31:34,920 --> 00:31:37,030
I could work my way
into this experimental class.

628
00:31:37,030 --> 00:31:38,070
Then people would stop saying

629
00:31:38,070 --> 00:31:39,920
Lin Zhixia's brother is a dumb brother.

630
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,400
-I...
-What a fool!

631
00:31:43,240 --> 00:31:44,030
You're too dumb to know

632
00:31:44,030 --> 00:31:46,960
the randomness and diversity
of gene combinations.

633
00:31:47,110 --> 00:31:48,960
You're so silly that you don't even know

634
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:50,920
how many strengths
and talents are in your genes.

635
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:52,070
You're so silly to think

636
00:31:52,070 --> 00:31:54,200
that you would embarrass your sister.

637
00:31:54,350 --> 00:31:55,350
So silly!

638
00:31:59,030 --> 00:32:00,480
I was just thinking,

639
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:02,000
if you had a brother

640
00:32:03,830 --> 00:32:04,830
who was smart,

641
00:32:05,750 --> 00:32:06,720
had a great personality,

642
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:07,550
played basketball well,

643
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:10,200
and wasn't totally ugly,

644
00:32:11,550 --> 00:32:12,880
you'd be pretty proud too, right?

645
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:15,540
Why would I think about
such impossible things?

646
00:32:18,400 --> 00:32:20,000
You'd better take that back.

647
00:32:22,200 --> 00:32:23,350
What I mean is,

648
00:32:24,830 --> 00:32:25,590
to me, you are already

649
00:32:25,590 --> 00:32:27,750
very, very, very excellent.

650
00:32:28,750 --> 00:32:30,070
I want to tell everyone

651
00:32:30,070 --> 00:32:31,750
that Lin Zeqiu is my brother.

652
00:32:31,880 --> 00:32:33,740
Not because you have good grades.

653
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,400
Not because
you are good at all kinds of sports.

654
00:32:36,400 --> 00:32:38,260
And not because you are handsome.

655
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,110
It's because you are

656
00:32:40,110 --> 00:32:42,480
the one and only Lin Zeqiu in this world,

657
00:32:42,920 --> 00:32:44,920
and the person who loves me the most.

658
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:50,960
I know.

659
00:32:51,070 --> 00:32:52,440
Don't cry, don't cry.

660
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,970
Why are you being so cheesy?

661
00:32:55,030 --> 00:32:55,890
No more crying.

662
00:32:56,350 --> 00:32:58,480
But you just wanted to cut ties with me!

663
00:32:58,550 --> 00:33:00,110
I just wanted to hear the truth from you

664
00:33:00,110 --> 00:33:01,200
and talk to you.

665
00:33:01,550 --> 00:33:03,680
I couldn't bear to erase those things.

666
00:33:05,550 --> 00:33:06,550
Is your hand okay?

667
00:33:07,270 --> 00:33:08,070
I fooled you.

668
00:33:09,510 --> 00:33:10,710
How dare you trick me?

669
00:33:11,110 --> 00:33:12,200
So what if I did?

670
00:33:13,270 --> 00:33:14,030
Apologize to me.

671
00:33:14,030 --> 00:33:15,200
Sorry.

672
00:33:15,550 --> 00:33:16,750
Not sincere enough.

673
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:24,880
Sorry, King Lin Zeqiu.

674
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:27,400
That's more like it.

675
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:29,480
I forgive you.

676
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:30,880
Let's draw it again.

677
00:33:30,880 --> 00:33:33,080
You erased the deer I drew when I was six.

678
00:33:33,830 --> 00:33:35,400
Look, I didn't erase it.

679
00:33:35,980 --> 00:33:38,000
You deliberately
rubbed against the wall just now,

680
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:39,510
-not the painting, right?
-Yeah.

681
00:33:39,510 --> 00:33:40,830
You are so smart.

682
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,000
I am so silly.

683
00:33:42,030 --> 00:33:43,440
I'm really so silly.

684
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:45,460
I totally missed that.

685
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,080
A little piece fell off here.

686
00:34:04,720 --> 00:34:05,780
Morning, Grandma.

687
00:34:06,110 --> 00:34:06,750
Morning.

688
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,409
Heading to school, Zhixia?

689
00:34:10,510 --> 00:34:11,550
Morning, Grandma Leng.

690
00:34:11,550 --> 00:34:12,190
Morning.

691
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:16,280
You just love teasing it.

692
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:17,590
Did you feed it?

693
00:34:18,710 --> 00:34:20,000
I did.

694
00:34:37,840 --> 00:34:39,440
Keep a distance of 10 meters.

695
00:34:39,480 --> 00:34:40,360
Don't talk to me.

696
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:41,550
No eye contact.

697
00:34:41,550 --> 00:34:43,409
Don't let others misunderstand.

698
00:35:01,230 --> 00:35:02,030
Lin Zhixia.

699
00:35:02,960 --> 00:35:04,220
Can you come to my side?

700
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:08,480
I don't have eyes on the back of my head.

701
00:35:08,480 --> 00:35:09,590
How can I watch you?

702
00:35:12,800 --> 00:35:13,480
Come here.

703
00:35:24,940 --> 00:35:25,630
Let's go.

704
00:35:33,910 --> 00:35:34,760
Lin Zeqiu.

705
00:35:34,760 --> 00:35:35,710
Is that Lin Zeqiu?

706
00:35:35,710 --> 00:35:36,440
Yeah.

707
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,890
What's going on? Let's go check it out.

708
00:35:40,320 --> 00:35:41,110
Lin Zeqiu.

709
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,070
Lin Zhixia.

710
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:45,190
Come here.

711
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:46,630
Come here.

712
00:35:48,030 --> 00:35:50,070
Lin Zhixia is my sister.

713
00:35:51,590 --> 00:35:52,850
Lin Zeqiu. Lin Zhixia.

714
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:54,920
No wonder the names are so similar.

715
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:55,840
Sorry.

716
00:35:56,070 --> 00:35:57,590
Your sister is just too outstanding.

717
00:35:57,590 --> 00:35:58,960
So we really couldn't

718
00:35:58,960 --> 00:36:00,360
associate you two together.

719
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,960
A well-known top student in school...

720
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:04,480
And an unknown ordinary person.

721
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,800
Are you blood-related?

722
00:36:06,800 --> 00:36:07,920
Were you adopted?

723
00:36:09,590 --> 00:36:12,120
Even if he was adopted,
he's still my brother.

724
00:36:13,190 --> 00:36:14,360
We're blood-related.

725
00:36:14,360 --> 00:36:15,620
We're blood-related.

726
00:36:15,960 --> 00:36:17,280
Why are you disowning me?

727
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:18,410
Human intelligence

728
00:36:18,550 --> 00:36:20,550
is 40 to 60 percent innate.

729
00:36:20,590 --> 00:36:22,250
And statistically speaking,

730
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:24,550
I probably benefited from
the law of conservation.

731
00:36:24,550 --> 00:36:26,320
My brother might not be a genius,

732
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:27,780
but he is very persistent.

733
00:36:29,030 --> 00:36:31,360
There was a math problem
that wasn't too hard before,

734
00:36:31,360 --> 00:36:33,070
but he refused to let me help him with it.

735
00:36:33,070 --> 00:36:35,000
He locked himself in his room
for two nights

736
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,530
and finally figured it out.

737
00:36:38,670 --> 00:36:41,200
What about you?
Are you as hardworking as him?

738
00:36:44,440 --> 00:36:46,240
Are you sure you're praising me?

739
00:36:52,360 --> 00:36:54,560
Although my brother always yells at me,

740
00:36:55,070 --> 00:36:55,920
I know

741
00:36:56,230 --> 00:36:57,630
he always cares about me.

742
00:36:57,920 --> 00:36:59,590
He'd give me his pocket money,

743
00:37:00,510 --> 00:37:01,960
claiming it was from my dad.

744
00:37:01,960 --> 00:37:04,710
My mom keeps track of
our family store's inventory.

745
00:37:04,710 --> 00:37:07,110
Every time he snuck strawberry milk for me

746
00:37:07,150 --> 00:37:08,480
and got caught by my mom,

747
00:37:08,550 --> 00:37:10,170
he'd take the blame
and say he wanted it himself.

748
00:37:10,170 --> 00:37:12,310
He took a lot of beatings for that.

749
00:37:12,880 --> 00:37:14,440
When I ran a fever,

750
00:37:14,590 --> 00:37:16,320
he'd quietly stand guard outside my room.

751
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:17,550
If anything happened,

752
00:37:17,550 --> 00:37:19,280
he'd rush in right away.

753
00:37:20,150 --> 00:37:21,230
He even washed

754
00:37:21,420 --> 00:37:22,960
my stuffed animals for me.

755
00:37:22,980 --> 00:37:23,880
What about you?

756
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:26,010
Do you have such a good brother?

757
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,880
Can you hear it?

758
00:37:33,280 --> 00:37:34,070
No, I can't.

759
00:37:35,630 --> 00:37:37,560
All right, we're just teasing you.

760
00:37:37,860 --> 00:37:38,670
Go ahead.

761
00:37:41,510 --> 00:37:42,040
Bye-bye.

762
00:37:43,510 --> 00:37:45,480
So your family runs a grocery store?

763
00:37:45,480 --> 00:37:46,980
Does that mean you have unlimited snacks

764
00:37:46,980 --> 00:37:47,650
and drinks?

765
00:37:47,920 --> 00:37:48,960
I'm so jealous!

766
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:50,780
Do you guys ever catch the point

767
00:37:50,780 --> 00:37:52,110
when people are talking?

768
00:37:52,110 --> 00:37:54,070
Actually, your sister is quite cute.

769
00:37:54,070 --> 00:37:55,730
I wish I had such a cute sister.

770
00:37:56,280 --> 00:37:58,610
You actually washed her stuffed animals?

771
00:38:37,630 --> 00:38:41,670
[Gold Award: Best Brother of the Nation]

772
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:52,580
[Gold Award: Best Brother of the Nation]
